counterfactuals.output:
A user equipment (UE) comprising one or more processors and memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the UE to perform operations comprising:

receiving, at a GPRS mobility management/session management (GMM/SM) protocol layer of the UE, an authentication and key agreement (AKA) request transmitted by a serving GPRS support node (SGSN);

processing the AKA request at the GMM/SM protocol layer to obtain authentication information including a message authentication code (MAC);

generating, by the UE, a verification key for authenticating the AKA request;

selecting, by the UE, an authentication algorithm from among a plurality of available authentication algorithms;

verifying the MAC using the generated verification key and the selected authentication algorithm; and

in response to successfully verifying the MAC, generating an AKA response and transmitting the AKA response from the UE to the SGSN.
